==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*fedwōr}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*kʷetwóres}}.

Common Germanic cognates include {{cog|goh|fior}} ({{cog|de|vier}}), {{cog|osx|fiuwar}}, {{cog|odt|viuwar}} ({{cog|nl|vier}}), {{cog|non|fjórir}}, {{cog|got|𐍆𐌹𐌳𐍅𐍉𐍂}}.

Indo-European cognates include Proto-Slavic {{m|sla-pro|*četyre}} (Russian {{l|ru|четыре}}), Old Irish [[cethair]], Greek {{m|grc|τέσσαρες}}, Latin ''[[quattuor]]''.

